# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# apps/academorix-family — per-project pnpm settings
#
# `node-linker=hoisted` tells pnpm to build a **flat, symlink-free**
# `node_modules/` tree for this project only. The rest of the
# workspace keeps pnpm's default linked layout (`.pnpm/` +
# per-package symlinks); the RN app gets a yarn-classic / npm-style
# tree where every dep is a single physical folder under
# `<app>/node_modules/<name>/`.
#
# Why: React Native's Metro bundler + React's context module
# identity both rely on ONE canonical install per package. pnpm's
# default `.pnpm/<pkg>@<version>_HASH` layout creates one folder
# per unique combination of resolved peer deps — meaning a single
# `heroui-native@1.0.5` can appear three times in `.pnpm/` (one
# per hash), each with its own `React.createContext()` object.
# Provider mounts context A → downstream `<Card>` reads context B
# → `useContext()` returns `undefined` → runtime crash:
#
#   TypeError: Cannot read property 'globalIsAllAnimationsDisabled'
#   of undefined
#     at HeroUINative.Surface.Root
#     at HeroUINative.Card.Root
#
# `node-linker=hoisted` sidesteps every one of those failure modes
# by giving Metro a truly flat tree — same layout `yarn install`
# would produce. React Native has no context-identity problems in a
# flat tree because there IS only one context object per package.
#
# See: https://pnpm.io/npmrc#node-linker
node-linker=hoisted
